 ## Background
-FLD was developed originally for radiative transfer applications in astrophysics [LP81, TS01] and nuclear physics [LK74] [S1]. It was introduced to computer graphics to improve the accuracy of multiple scattering simulations in heterogeneous media [S1].
+FLD was developed originally for radiative transfer applications in astrophysics [LP81, TS01] and nuclear physics [LK74] [S1]. Applied to computer graphics for multiple scattering in participating media, it extends the theoretical framework of CDA by replacing the diffusion coefficient with a $\phi(\mathbf{x})$-dependent expression [S1].
 
